'''{{D|Corrosive}} Damage''' is one of the six secondary elemental damage types, composed of {{D|Toxin}} and {{D|Electricity}} damage. Deals increased damage to {{D|Grineer}}, {{D|Kuva Grineer}}, and {{D|Scaldra}}, but reduced damage against {{D|Sentient}}. Its [[Status Effect]] temporarily degrades enemy [[Armor]].

==[[Status Effect]]s==
===General===
The status effect of {{D|Corrosive}} damage is '''Corrosion'''. It temporarily degrades the [[armor]] of the afflicted target by '''26%''' for '''8''' seconds. Subsequent procs further reduce armor by '''6%''', culminating in a total armor reduction of '''80%''' at '''10''' stacks, with each stack having its own duration. Any stacks applied after the 10th will replace the oldest stack.

{{Resource|Emerald Archon Shard}} can increase the maximum {{D|Corrosive}} status procs by '''+2''' ('''+3''' for {{Resource|Tauforged Emerald Archon Shard|Tauforged}}). Applying '''14''' stacks can fully remove all armor for the duration of the status.

Against an enemy with capped armor, giving 90% [[Armor#Enemy Damage Reduction Formula|damage reduction]] (such as level 57 [[Heavy Gunner]]), one stack of '''Corrosion''' will give an effective damage increase of approximately '''x2.3''' (or '''+130%'''). Each subsequent stack will give a ranging incremental effective damage increase, starting at approximately '''+32%''', and ending at '''+56%'''. 10 stacks of '''Corrosion''' give an approximately '''x6''' (or '''+500%''') effective damage increase. In comparison to 10 stacks of '''Corrosion''', 14 stacks would give '''~x1.67''' relative effective damage increase.<ref>https://www.desmos.com/calculator/oqldvpbsuc</ref>

{{WF|Hydroid}}'s [[Hydroid/Abilities#Passive|passive]] causes enemies damaged by him to be permanently more vulnerable to {{D|Corrosive}} status, with the first proc degrading '''50%''' of armor, allowing him to have '''100%''' armor reduction at 10 stacks. This vulnerability can come from any source of {{D|Corrosive}} procs, not just from Hydroid's weapons or abilities, as long as he has damaged the enemy.

Enemies affected by a {{D|Corrosive}} proc will be covered in a faint green, electricity-like substance. Enemies killed while affected by a {{D|Corrosive}} proc will have their corpses partially corroded and dissolved.

{{D|Corrosive}} status [[armor]] reduction is '''multiplicative''' with other armor reduction sources. This can be expressed as the following: <br/>
{{MathText|Armor after reduction {{eql}} (1 - {{Tooltip|50%|Heat status max armor reduction of 50% after 2 seconds.}}) {{mul}} [1 - ({{Tooltip|20%|Innate Corrosive status armor reduction.}} + {{Tooltip|6%|Corrosive status armor reduction of 6% per stack.}} {{mul}} Number of Corrosive stacks)] {{mul}} (1 - {{Tooltip|18%|18% armor reduction from one max-rank Corrosive Projection.}} {{mul}} Number Corrosive Projections)}}

{{CustomCollapsible|View  detailed examples|ARI|&nbsp;}}
For example, a full 4-player squad with max-rank {{M|Corrosive Projection|Corrosive Projections}}, an active {{D|Heat}} proc, and max stacked {{D|Corrosive}} proc will result in an enemy's armor being reduced to:
:{{Math| (1 - 50%) {{mul}} [1 - (20% + 6% {{mul}} 10)] {{mul}} (1 - 18% {{mul}} 4)|mt=y|p=y}}.

If only one player has a max-rank {{M|Corrosive Projection}} with the above statuses, an enemy's armor would instead be reduced to:
:{{Math| (1 - 50%) {{mul}} [1 - (20% + 6% {{mul}} 10)] {{mul}} (1 - 18%)|mt=y|p=y}}.

An active {{D|Heat}} proc, and max stacked {{D|Corrosive}} proc ''without'' {{M|Corrosive Projection}} would result in an enemy's armor being reduced to:
:{{Math| (1 - 50%) {{mul}} [1 - (20% + 6% {{mul}} 10)]|mt=y|p=y}}.

Currently, the only non-[[Abilities|ability]] method to ''completely'' remove armor is to use {{M|Shattering Impact}}, {{M|Sharpened Claws}} or a [[dagger]] in tandem with {{M|Amalgam Argonak Metal Auger}}.
{{CustomCollapsible/End}}

===Railjack===
{{D|Corrosive}} does not have a [[Railjack]] space counterpart and is thus not able to proc any status effect nor is it included in calculations for status proc weighting.

